<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yusuf Dey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1637</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yusuf Dey was dey of Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a> from 1610 to 1637, the most powerful official of the regency in his time. He welcomed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moriscos">Morisco</a> refugees expelled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, who founded and settled towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/testour">Testour</a>, and he encouraged corsairing and trade. His mosque in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>, built in the 1610s, was the first in the city in the Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanafi-school">Hanafi</a> style.</p></div>
